Laboratory Safety for Chemistry Students — Hill and Finster, third edition (@gc-acsadvanced: 0, is #reference, #part-of @gc-sources) { r_7TD6AG2TZZ0GS0EWJMC8KC9SB0
Robert H. Hill Jr. and David C. Finster. Laboratory Safety for Chemistry Students, third edition, made available through the American Chemical Society. [Official access, chapter overview, and registration information](https://institute.acs.org/etextbook).

Use the complete textbook as the sustained safety reading for practical and research work. It develops introductory, intermediate, and advanced sections across eight chapters: culture, information resources, health hazards, physical hazards, risk assessment, operations, waste/storage, and emergencies. Match the actual experiment with the relevant sections and current local procedures.

The official page states free eTextbook access for students/instructors, requiring a free ACS ID and a short registration form. This is conditional free access, not an asserted Creative Commons redistribution licence. The public chapter overview was inspected; the registered full platform was not accessed or represented as tested. Availability, authors, access conditions, and stated structure checked on 29 October 2026. ACS's openly accessible student booklet provides an immediate first reading without registration. No account is created or book copied by this trail.

